THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because the parameter is annotated @Nullable but then dereferenced without a null check. To fix only this error without changing behavior elsewhere, I’ll add an explicit null check that throws a NullPointerException if color is null, which matches typical expectations for such setters and avoids introducing new errors. Then I should run the compile to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '117,122c\  public Color set(@Nullable Color color) {
    if (color == null) {
      throw new NullPointerException("color cannot be null");
    }
    this.r = color.r;
    this.g = color.g;
    this.b = color.b;
    this.a = color.a;
    return this;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/Color.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

